 & 12 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11k & 12k \\\\ 4k & -8k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the matrix given for $kB$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}11k & 12k \\\\ -4k & -8k\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}33 & 36 \\\\ -12 & -24\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the bottom-left elements, $-4k$ and $-12.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4k & =-12 \\\\ k & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements." 13194139535480 17592186045443 false] [17592186299853 1074 "To express $kB,$ we multiply each entry of $B$ by $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kB & =k\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 12 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11k & 12k \\\\ 4k & -8k\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the matrix given for $kB$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}11k & 12k \\\\ -4k & -8k\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}33 & 36 \\\\ -12 & -24\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the bottom-left elements, $-4k$ and $-12.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4k & =-12 \\\\ k & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements." 13194139535480 17592186045443 true] [17592186299854 1074 "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} & a \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} & a \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 6-a\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =9+5a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, setting the expression for the dete